{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Hey, I\u2019m making Landmaster \u2013 a pixel-art RPG where you get tossed into a big, living world full of strange creatures and secrets waiting to be found. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It\u2019s a mix of survival, crafting, and building: </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Gather resources and craft tools, weapons, and magical artifacts</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Build and defend your base against dangers that lurk in the Kingdom</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore different biomes, from quiet forests to dangerous ruins </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Unravel the mystery of an ancient curse that\u2019s tearing the land apart </p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >I wanted Landmaster to feel like one big adventure, where every day can surprise you. One evening you might be fixing your base after an attack, the next you\u2019re discovering a forgotten cave or making choices that shape the fate of the Kingdom. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game is still in a super early stage. It\u2019s buggy, there\u2019s not a ton of content yet, and things will break. But I\u2019m working on it every single day, and I want to share the progress with players as it grows. Landmaster is not finished, but if you like the idea of exploring, building, and surviving in a weird little pixel world\u2014and you don\u2019t mind rough edges\u2014you\u2019re very welcome to join in early.</p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/2848680?t=1760110184","background_raw":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2848680/67e014276305766fc36f865e623eb060b3d7f746/page_bg_raw.jpg?t=1760110184","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2848680/5efbd90d8ab12ab4289a3567004c7d4ca32c24cb/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1760110184","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2848680/5efbd90d8ab12ab4289a3567004c7d4ca32c24cb/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1760110184","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[],"notes":null},"detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Hey, I\u2019m making Landmaster \u2013 a pixel-art RPG where you get tossed into a big, living world full of strange creatures and secrets waiting to be found. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It\u2019s a mix of survival, crafting, and building: </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Gather resources and craft tools, weapons, and magical artifacts</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Build and defend your base against dangers that lurk in the Kingdom</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore different biomes, from quiet forests to dangerous ruins </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Unravel the mystery of an ancient curse that\u2019s tearing the land apart </p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >I wanted Landmaster to feel like one big adventure, where every day can surprise you. One evening you might be fixing your base after an attack, the next you\u2019re discovering a forgotten cave or making choices that shape the fate of the Kingdom. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game is still in a super early stage. It\u2019s buggy, there\u2019s not a ton of content yet, and things will break. But I\u2019m working on it every single day, and I want to share the progress with players as it grows. Landmaster is not finished, but if you like the idea of exploring, building, and surviving in a weird little pixel world\u2014and you don\u2019t mind rough edges\u2014you\u2019re very welcome to join in early.</p>","developer